# G8 Flow — Page architecture

Single marketing homepage. Sections in this order only unless the user reorders.

## S1 — Hero (sales + SEO, Hormozi voice)

- Outcome-led H1 (never stuff “websites / apps / SaaS” as the H1 keyword dump). Aim: site that earns for the business.
- Short supporting line; whole site copy shows how work grows client revenue.
- Exactly **2 CTA buttons**.
- Personal photo → scroll-driven dissolve into glowing white particles/stars (GSAP ScrollTrigger + Canvas/WebGL), particles carry into S2 and reform as a 3D object filling empty S2 space.
- Refs: originkit dot-image-reveal, particles.casberry, premium Apple/Awwwards motion, 60fps, mobile-safe, lazy-load heavy FX.

## S2 — Process (“The Flux way” pattern)

- Inspiration: Flux Academy “The Flux way” — clear path from project start → launch.
- Adapt to G8 Flow delivery steps (not Flux course marketing).

## S3 — Featured work

- Inspiration: https://konvo.pk/ “Picture” section energy.
- Left: site name + logo. Right: idea + business outcomes achieved.
- Media: autoplay scroll-through of the live site (not Konvo’s video).
- Cases: (1) https://busystrong90.com/ (2) https://lenkolino.shop/ (3) https://thrivewithmarina.vercel.app/

## S4 — Testimonials (coverflow)

- Base: Originkit Coverflow / Smooth3DSlideshow (`docs/g8-flow/references/coverflow-testimonials.tsx`).
- When a face is active, show **name + humanized review** below (not only title on card).
- `showTitle` can be false on cards if name/quote live under the stage.

## S5 — Pricing (3 plans)

- Three clear plans; each states business-value outcomes (revenue/leads/clarity), not feature dumps.
- Highlight one recommended plan.

## S6 — CTA band

- Match prior site visual language; optional inspiration from Flowninja-style CTA sections.
- One primary action; optional secondary.

## S7 — Footer

- Layout inspiration: https://capsules.moyra.co/
- Restyle with G8 Flow colors; brand **G8 Flow**.

## Frontend design constraints

Follow the user’s frontend design user-rules (hero budget, no hero cards/overlays, one job per section, real visual anchors, intentional motion 2–3×).
